    win:
      perform intern_conclave +small
      arcana +small
      say: {The spell works on the first try. Behind the glass, someone writes your name in the margin of their notes.|It works, more or less, for one glorious minute before the spell remembers itself.|The spell works, and nobody behind the glass will say what it was for. They thank you very politely.}
    lose:
      health -small
      perform intern_conclave -tiny
      say: {The spell goes off sideways. Your eyebrows are fine. Your fringe has views of its own now.|The spell goes off sideways, and your robes will never fold the same way again.|The spell goes off sideways and adds a new scorch mark to the wall. Someone labels it with your name.}
> right: Take readings behind the glass
  wage
  arcana +tiny
  perform intern_conclave +tiny
  mood -small
  say: {You write down numbers for three hours while someone else gets to be brave. They're very good numbers.|You note every flicker. A senior researcher reads your page and asks for your notes next time.|You take the readings for a spell nobody will name. The numbers are strange, and you're asked to forget them.}

@event intern_conclave_minutes
