    perform intern_conclave +small
    renown +tiny
    mood -tiny
    say: {The table goes silent. Then the oldest mage says, "The intern is right," and the rest pretend they agreed all along.|Your opinion settles the argument. It also starts two new ones.|You give your opinion and the sleeper wakes up to agree with it. It carries, seven to two.}
  else:
    perform intern_conclave -tiny
    mood -small
    say: {Nine heads turn towards you, slowly. You say something about wands. It isn't minuted.|You give your opinion and it is recorded in full, with the note "(intern)".|Your opinion is noted, discussed, voted down and then adopted next meeting without credit.}
> right: Keep my head down and write
  wage
  perform intern_conclave +small
  lore +tiny
  mood -small
  say: {Your minutes are perfect and so dull that nobody reads them, which in a committee is the highest praise.|You record every word of the argument. Your hand aches, and you understand the Conclave much better than you wanted to.|You write it all down, including the vote of the member who slept through it. The minutes are accurate, which nobody wanted.}

# ---------------- Internship: the Guild of Alchemists' Works ----------------

@event intern_alchemists_vat_watch
title: Vat Watch
track: intern_alchemists
class: routine
