tags: study
scene: A huge copper vat in a steaming hall, a student on a gantry staring into it with a colour chart in hand.
text: {Your task at the works is to watch one great vat and call the foreman if it changes colour.|You've brought your own colour chart now, with notes in the margins.|You and the vat understand each other now. It's an unsettling feeling.} {The amber is drifting, very slowly.|There's a bubble that keeps coming back, like a thought.|The vat smells faintly of cinnamon, which it never has before.} The foreman is all the way at the other end of the hall.
> left: Adjust it myself
  wage
  challenge brew adept-:
    win:
      perform intern_alchemists +small
      alchemy +small
      say: {A pinch of salt and a slow stir, and the vat settles back to its proper self. The foreman never knew, but the vat did.|You correct it before it goes wrong. When the foreman passes, he gives the vat a satisfied look as if he did it.|You trace the cinnamon to a cracked spice valve and close it. The vat settles, and the foreman finds the valve next week.}
    lose:
      perform intern_alchemists -small
      health -tiny
      say: {The vat turns a brilliant violet and hisses. The foreman arrives at a run, and you'll be hearing about it for weeks.|You add too much salt. The vat sulks a muddy brown until the foreman coaxes it back, at length, with you watching.|You make it worse. A lot worse. The whole hall smells of cinnamon until the end of the week.}
> right: Run for the foreman
  wage
  perform intern_alchemists +tiny
  alchemy +tiny
  mood -small
  health -tiny
  say: {You run the length of the hall. The foreman fixes it in a second and explains how, at length, as you catch your breath.|By the time you're back with the foreman the colour has corrected itself. He stares at you, then at the vat.|You run for the foreman, who sniffs the air, says "Cinnamon," and goes very pale. He fixes it, and doesn't explain.}

@event intern_alchemists_no_flame
title: The Rule About Flames
track: intern_alchemists
class: routine
