art: cup
tags: study
scene: A break room in an alchemical works, workers gathered around a kettle sitting on a glowing stone that is not, technically, on fire.
text: {There's a strict rule at the works against naked flames, and against any heating reaction the foreman hasn't approved. The break room has spent forty years looking for one he will.|Break time. The kettle sits on its warm stone, and the workers look at you hopefully.|By now the break room asks the academy intern first, whatever the problem.} {Today the warm stone has gone cold.|Today someone wants toast, which is a much bigger question.|Today a new inspector is touring the works.}
> left: Help brew the flameless tea
  wage
  chance likely:
    alchemy +small
    mood +small
    say: {You heat the kettle with a reaction you learned in your first year. The break room calls it "the academy method" and adopts it on the spot.|It works, though everything boiled on it comes out a little purple.|You brew the tea with the new inspector in the room, and explain the method so confidently that he takes notes.}
  else:
    perform intern_alchemists -small
    mood -tiny
    say: {Your method works so well that someone in charge notices the steam from a reaction nobody approved. There's a meeting about it, with you in it.|The kettle boils, and so, briefly, does the table.|The inspector walks in mid-reaction. There's a form for it, and you fill it in.}
> right: Stick to the rules
  wage
  perform intern_alchemists +tiny
  mood -small
  say: {You drink cold water while everyone else drinks tea brewed on an unapproved reaction. The foreman notes your conduct, and the break room notes it too.|You remind everyone of the rule. You are absolutely right and nobody offers you a biscuit for the rest of the week.|You keep to the rules with the inspector watching. He commends you by name, and the break room never forgives it.}

