text: {Each morning your Thornwick hosts leave pastries on your desk, with a polite note.|The notes have grown longer and politer, which is worrying.|The pastries are a game now, and both sides know it.} {They look perfect, which in an illusion lab is a warning.|One is steaming slightly, which it shouldn't be.|Today there's one plain biscuit, which is somehow worse.} {season == "winter": The pastries look very warm.|The icing hasn't melted in the heat.}
