  challenge negotiate adept-:
    win:
      perform intern_thornwick +small
      charm +small
      say: {You answer every barb with a better one. By lunch they're laughing with you rather than at you.|You make the room laugh at their joke, and then at them. Their supervisor smiles behind her notes.|You do a better impression of them than they did of you. The lab agrees, and so, grudgingly, do they.}
    lose:
      mood -small
      perform intern_thornwick -tiny
      say: {You try to be witty. It comes out as a speech about the founders. They let you finish, kindly.|You lose the exchange so badly that one of them takes a bow on your behalf.|Their impression of you is so good that you forget your answer. They finish it for you, in your voice.}
> right: Let it slide
  wage
  perform intern_thornwick +tiny
  mood -small
  say: {You smile and go back to work. Your supervisor here notices, and approves, and you feel like you lost anyway.|You say nothing. It takes them all morning to realise you've won.|You let it go, as usual. They seem almost disappointed, and one of them saves you a seat at lunch.}

# ---------------- Internship: the Office of Unseen Affairs ----------------

@event intern_unseen_office_coffee
title: The Coffee Machine
track: intern_unseen_office
class: routine
tone: eerie
repeat: 5
weight: 10
art: cup
tags: study mystery
scene: A plain room with no windows and a gleaming coffee machine, quiet people in plain coats standing near it, not quite talking.
text: {Nobody at the Office talks about anything, except the coffee machine. It's very good.|A queue forms around the machine each evening, though nobody seems to join it.|The coffee queue, you've learned, is where the Office's real work gets done.} {Two people beside you discuss the weather in a way that isn't about the weather.|A cup has a name on it that was there yesterday, under another name.|The machine hisses, and everyone falls silent until it stops.}
> left: Linger at the machine
  wage
  chance likely:
    guile +small
    perform intern_unseen_office +tiny
    say: {You learn three things nobody told you, and one thing nobody knows you know.|You drink your coffee slowly and listen. By the second cup you understand what nobody is saying.|You stand in the queue long enough to be part of it. Someone tells you something, and you understand it was meant for you.}
  else:
    mood -small
    say: {Someone notices you listening and asks, very kindly, how your day is going. You don't sleep that night.|You overhear something you very much wish you hadn't. It can't be unheard.|The machine hisses mid-sentence and the room goes silent. When it stops, everyone is looking at you.}
> right: Take my cup back to my desk
  wage
  perform intern_unseen_office +small
  mood -small
  say: {You work through the evening with your coffee. The work is dull and your supervisor approves, which is a little chilling.|Your desk is very quiet. It's the most anyone at the Office will say about you, and here that's high praise.|You take your cup to your desk. When you come back for the next one, the queue has saved your place.}

@event intern_unseen_office_wrong_file
title: The Wrong File
track: intern_unseen_office
class: routine
tone: eerie
repeat: 5
weight: 10
art: eye
tags: study mystery
scene: A plain folder with no label lying on an empty desk under a single lamp.
text: {A file has been left on your desk. It isn't yours, and it isn't labelled.|A second unlabelled file. You're starting to think it's a test.|The unlabelled files keep arriving. You've stopped asking where they come from.} This one is tied shut with a red ribbon. {It's very thin.|It's very thick, with a coffee ring on the cover.|The knot is one you don't recognise.}
> left: Read it before returning it
  wage
  alignment -tiny
  challenge deceive adept-:
    win:
      guile +small
      perform intern_unseen_office +small
      say: {You read it, retie the ribbon perfectly and hand it in. Your supervisor checks the knot and smiles, very slightly.|You read every page. It's about a man who sells hats. Nothing has ever made you more nervous.|You read it, retie the unfamiliar knot from memory and hand it in. Your supervisor checks it twice and then teaches you a new one.}
    lose:
      perform intern_unseen_office -small
      mood -tiny
      say: {Your supervisor takes the file back and glances at the ribbon. "Interesting knot," she says.|You put the pages back in the wrong order. Somehow, everyone knows by morning.|You can't retie the knot. You hand it in with an ordinary bow, and your supervisor looks at it for a long time.}
> right: Return it unopened
  wage
  alignment +tiny
  perform intern_unseen_office +tiny
  mood -small
  say: {You hand it back without looking. Your supervisor says nothing, which here is approval. You'll wonder about it for weeks.|You return it with the ribbon untouched. The next day there's a slightly better coffee waiting on your desk.|You return it unopened, as always. The files stop coming for a week, and then there are two.}
